From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:14:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tools: Start SpotPass Tasks Right Away (Build 137)

The real SpotPass module (boss) runs a game's tasks on the game's own
schedule; Nintendogs + Cats checks for a SpotPass neighbour every 12
hours, so testing a new file on the server meant waiting half a day.

Tools > Start SpotPass Tasks Right Away (a tick, off at every start):
while it is on, a game's own boss:U request that names one of its tasks
(StartTask 0x001C, UpdateTaskInterval 0x0017, UpdateTaskCount 0x0018) is
passed to boss as StartTaskImmediate (0x001D0042: size, task ID buffer)
for the same task, and boss's reply goes back to the game under the
command it sent. All of them answer with just a result. Nintendogs
names its task once at start (UpdateTaskCount task_EU), so: tick the
option, start the game, and the task runs straight away. The task count
or interval the game sent is dropped that one time (it sends it again
at its next start). Each task is started this way at most once a
minute. Logged on Service.BOSS Info: "SpotPass: <game> names its task
<id> ...: starting it right away" and boss's answer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
